My only ever ascension was genoless, but I'd still agree that titans are
worse than boss liches.  Even though the liches have higher base level,
they seem to cast Summon Nasties far less often.

I think the liches are actually weaker *because* they have tactical
teleport.  When encountering a titan, you need to spend turns approaching
him, and during that time most of his spells besides summoning aren't
applicable.  Worse, a cloud of nasties can stall you from reaching
adjacency, giving him time to do it again.

Boss liches, however, are always either in your face or far away.  They
take about one blow from you for each time they cast, and whenever Summon
Nasties is available, so are all the other spells.

